.TH V7LD 1 "August 2026" "V7 toolchain" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v7ld \- V7 PDP-11 loader (host-ported)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v7ld
[ option ] file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I v7ld
combines several object programs into one, resolves external
references, and searches libraries.  It produces a V7
.I a.out
(magic 0407).  In the simplest case several object files are given and
combined into an executable; with
.B \-r
the result preserves relocation bits for a further
.I v7ld
run.
.PP
Arguments are concatenated in order; the entry point is the beginning
of the first routine.  A library is searched exactly once, at the point
it appears in the argument list; only the members defining an unresolved
external are loaded.  If the first member is named
.B __.SYMDEF
it is used as a dictionary (as produced by
.IR ranlib ).
.PP
The symbols
.BR _etext ,
.BR _edata
and
.BR _end
are reserved and set to the end of text, initialized data, and all data
respectively.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s
Strip the output (remove the symbol table and relocation bits).
.TP
.BI \-u " symbol"
Enter
.I symbol
as undefined in the symbol table.
.TP
.BI \-l " x"
Abbreviation for the library
.RI lib x .a ;
searched in each
.B \-L
directory, then
.BR /lib ,
then
.BR /usr/lib .
.TP
.BI \-L " dir"
Search
.I dir
for
.B \-l
libraries before the default directories.  (A host-port addition; V7's
loader had no
.BR \-L .)
.TP
.B \-x
Do not preserve local (non-.globl) symbols in the output symbol table.
.TP
.B \-X
Save local symbols except those beginning with
.BR L .
.TP
.B \-r
Generate relocation bits in the output; suppress undefined-symbol
diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-d
Force definition of common storage even with
.BR \-r .
.TP
.B \-n
Make the text read-only and shared (move data to the next 4K boundary).
.TP
.B \-i
Separate I/D address spaces (data starts at location 0).
.TP
.BI \-o " name"
Use
.I name
as the output file instead of
.BR a.out .
.TP
.BI \-e " name"
Set the entry point.
.TP
.B \-O
Overlay file; only the text segment will be replaced by exec(2).
.TP
.BI \-D " num"
Set the data segment size.
.SH FILES
.ta \w'/usr/local/lib/pdp11-v7/  'u
/lib/lib*.a	searched libraries
.br
/usr/lib/lib*.a	more libraries
.br
/usr/local/lib/pdp11-v7/lib*.a	target libraries
.br
a.out	output file
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR v7as (1),
.IR v7cc (1),
.IR ar (1),
.IR ranlib (1)
.SH BUGS
The library-name buffer is host-fixed at 512 bytes (V7 wrote into a
read-only string literal, which segfaults on a modern host); very long
.I name
arguments are not supported.
